# ~/.zshenv — root-owned on source machine (mode 600, owned by root).
# On the source machine this file is unreadable by the normal user, so its
# exact content cannot be copied here. Fix ownership with:
#   sudo chown $(id -u):$(id -g) ~/.zshenv
# then review its contents and copy them into this file if you want them
# shipped. Keep it minimal: zshenv is sourced on every zsh invocation.
